<?xml version="1.0"?>
<?xml-stylesheet type="text/xsl" href="http://jsbsim.sf.net/JSBSimScript.xsl"?>
<runscript
       name="Mi-17 15-minute hover"
       xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
       xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="http://jsbsim.sf.net/JSBSimScript.xsd">

  <description>
    Rewritten from scratch for the corrected main rotor (real Mi-17
    diameter/blade-count/chord, aircraft/mi17/Engines/mi17_main_
    rotor.xml). The previous version of this script (tuned for the
    old, undersized 52 ft/3-blade rotor placeholder) raised collective
    from 0.0 to 0.90 in a single instantaneous step at t=15s; against
    the corrected rotor's much higher thrust sensitivity (thrust scales
    roughly with numblades x chord x radius^3 in FGRotor's model) it
    did climb out and pass the altitude-hold handoff, but then
    diverged and crashed around t=34.5s during free flight, with no
    error message -- see this branch's commit history for the full
    investigation. Two concrete, data-backed changes made here instead
    of just re-tuning constants:

    1. Ground settle time extended from a guessed 15s to a measured
       120s: scripts/test_mi17_ground_run_idle.xml (governor-driven,
       no forced throttle) showed shaft-rpm only reaching ~187 RPM at
       30s and not actually converging to the 192 RPM target until
       ~90-120s. Raising collective while the governor is still
       fighting a large RPM error compounds two transients instead of
       letting one settle before starting the next.

    2. Collective is raised via a slow linear FG_RAMP (45s) instead of
       an instantaneous step, on the general principle that a real
       pilot does not slam the collective and a gradual input gives
       the rotor's inflow dynamics (already known borderline
       underdamped; see mi17_main_rotor.xml's inflowlag comment) more
       time to track rather than being hit with a step input. This is
       a reasonable, physically-motivated change, not a proven fix --
       the previous crash happened well after the (instantaneous) step
       was complete and liftoff had already occurred, during ordinary
       free flight, so a slower ramp may not address the actual root
       cause. Treat this run's outcome as new diagnostic data, not a
       validated solution.

    Collective-bias is zeroed for the entire ground-settle window (the
    fix validated in this branch's history: the corrected rotor
    produces ~19000-20000 lbs from the default 0.15 rad bias ALONE
    during the RPM-overshoot transient at engine start), and is itself
    ramped back to 0.15 (20s, t=120-140s) rather than restored as a
    step once the settle window ends -- an earlier cut of this rewrite
    ramped collective-cmd-norm but still restored collective-bias as an
    instantaneous step, reproducing the same abrupt-0.15-rad-jump
    mechanism at t=120s instead of engine start and triggering a
    catastrophic blowup (KCAS ~306, all four gear units cycling WOW
    within 7.5ms) within 6 seconds. The collective-cmd-norm ramp to the
    climb value (0.75, t=140-185s) only starts once the bias ramp is
    done. The climb-out target of 0.75 and the post-liftoff backoff
    target of 0.68 are unvalidated estimates, not measurements -- this
    model does not yet have a re-derived trim point for the corrected
    rotor. Checkpoints are frequent (10-20s) through the settle/ramp/
    climb-out phases specifically so that if this run also diverges,
    the trace shows where and how, rather than just a silent stop like
    the previous version's.
  </description>

  <use aircraft="mi17" initialize="reset00"/>

  <run start="0.0" end="1320.0" dt="0.0075">

    <event name="start" persistent="false">
      <condition> simulation/sim-time-sec ge 0.0 </condition>
      <set name="propulsion/set-running" value="-1"/>
      <set name="fcs/collective-cmd-norm" value="0.0"/>
      <set name="fcs/adj/collective-bias" value="0.0"/>
      <set name="ap/attitude-hold-on" value="1.0"/>
    </event>

    <event name="hold-attitude" persistent="true">
      <condition> simulation/sim-time-sec ge 0.0 </condition>
      <set name="ap/attitude-hold-on" value="1.0"/>
    </event>

    <event name="hold-ground-settle" persistent="true">
      <!-- 120s, not a guess: scripts/test_mi17_ground_run_idle.xml
           measured the governor actually converging to target-rpm in
           this window (shaft-rpm 187.0 at 30s, 191.6 at 60s, 192.0 by
           90-120s) with this same corrected rotor. -->
      <condition> simulation/sim-time-sec le 119.999 </condition>
      <set name="fcs/collective-cmd-norm" value="0.0"/>
      <set name="fcs/adj/collective-bias" value="0.0"/>
    </event>

    <event name="ramp-collective-bias" persistent="false">
      <!-- The first cut of this rewrite still restored collective-bias
           as an instantaneous 0.0 -> 0.15 rad step at t=120s (only the
           collective-cmd-norm portion was ramped); that reproduced the
           exact same abrupt-0.15-rad-jump mechanism already diagnosed
           as dangerous for this rotor (see the collective-cmd-norm
           ramp comment below), just moved later; it triggered a
           catastrophic blowup (KCAS ~306, all four gear units cycling
           WOW within a 7.5ms window) within 6 seconds, at t~126s.
           Ramping the bias itself, not just cmd-norm, fixes that. -->
      <condition> simulation/sim-time-sec ge 120.0 </condition>
      <set name="fcs/adj/collective-bias" value="0.15" action="FG_RAMP" tc="20.0"/>
      <notify>
        <property> simulation/sim-time-sec </property>
        <property> propulsion/gearbox[0]/shaft-rpm </property>
        <property> propulsion/engine[0]/n1 </property>
        <property> position/h-agl-ft </property>
      </notify>
    </event>

    <event name="ramp collective to climb" persistent="false">
      <!-- Starts once the bias ramp above has finished (140s), so the
           two ramps do not stack into a faster combined rate. Linear
           ramp (not a step) from 0.0 to 0.75 over 45s; see the
           description's rationale. 0.75 is an unvalidated estimate
           for the corrected rotor, not a measured trim value. -->
      <condition> simulation/sim-time-sec ge 140.0 </condition>
      <set name="fcs/collective-cmd-norm" value="0.75" action="FG_RAMP" tc="45.0"/>
    </event>

    <event name="checkpoint mid-bias-ramp (130s)" persistent="false">
      <condition> simulation/sim-time-sec ge 130.0 </condition>
      <notify>
        <property> simulation/sim-time-sec </property>
        <property> fcs/adj/collective-bias </property>
        <property> propulsion/engine[0]/collective-ctrl-rad </property>
        <property> propulsion/engine[0]/thrust-lbs </property>
        <property> position/h-agl-ft </property>
        <property> velocities/v-down-fps </property>
        <property> velocities/r-rad_sec </property>
      </notify>
    </event>

    <event name="checkpoint mid-ramp (165s)" persistent="false">
      <condition> simulation/sim-time-sec ge 165.0 </condition>
      <notify>
        <property> simulation/sim-time-sec </property>
        <property> fcs/collective-cmd-norm </property>
        <property> propulsion/engine[0]/collective-ctrl-rad </property>
        <property> propulsion/engine[0]/thrust-lbs </property>
        <property> position/h-agl-ft </property>
        <property> velocities/v-down-fps </property>
        <property> attitude/pitch-rad </property>
        <property> attitude/roll-rad </property>
        <property> velocities/r-rad_sec </property>
      </notify>
    </event>

    <event name="checkpoint ramp-complete (185s)" persistent="false">
      <condition> simulation/sim-time-sec ge 185.0 </condition>
      <notify>
        <property> simulation/sim-time-sec </property>
        <property> fcs/collective-cmd-norm </property>
        <property> propulsion/engine[0]/collective-ctrl-rad </property>
        <property> propulsion/engine[0]/thrust-lbs </property>
        <property> position/h-agl-ft </property>
        <property> velocities/v-down-fps </property>
        <property> attitude/pitch-rad </property>
        <property> attitude/roll-rad </property>
        <property> velocities/r-rad_sec </property>
      </notify>
    </event>

    <event name="checkpoint 200s" persistent="false">
      <condition> simulation/sim-time-sec ge 200.0 </condition>
      <notify>
        <property> simulation/sim-time-sec </property>
        <property> position/h-agl-ft </property>
        <property> velocities/v-down-fps </property>
        <property> attitude/pitch-rad </property>
        <property> attitude/roll-rad </property>
        <property> velocities/r-rad_sec </property>
      </notify>
    </event>

    <event name="checkpoint 215s" persistent="false">
      <condition> simulation/sim-time-sec ge 215.0 </condition>
      <notify>
        <property> simulation/sim-time-sec </property>
        <property> position/h-agl-ft </property>
        <property> velocities/v-down-fps </property>
        <property> attitude/pitch-rad </property>
        <property> attitude/roll-rad </property>
        <property> velocities/r-rad_sec </property>
      </notify>
    </event>

    <event name="engage altitude hold, ramp collective back toward trim" persistent="false">
      <!-- Gated on both a real climb (h-agl-ft ge 15) and being past
           the ramp-complete time, same guard against the initial
           ground-touchdown mechanical bounce as the previous version
           of this script used. Backoff is also a ramp (10s), not a
           step, to 0.68; again an unvalidated estimate, chosen
           slightly below the 0.75 climb value on the assumption (not
           yet confirmed for this rotor) that trim sits somewhat below
           climb power, matching the general shape of the old rotor's
           now-invalid 0.90/0.72 pair. -->
      <condition>
        simulation/sim-time-sec ge 185.0
        position/h-agl-ft ge 15.0
      </condition>
      <set name="ap/altitude-target-ft" value="2313.5"/>
      <set name="ap/altitude-hold-on" value="1.0"/>
      <set name="fcs/collective-cmd-norm" value="0.68" action="FG_RAMP" tc="10.0"/>
      <notify>
        <property> simulation/sim-time-sec </property>
        <property> position/h-agl-ft </property>
        <property> velocities/v-down-fps </property>
      </notify>
    </event>

    <event name="hold-altitude-mode" persistent="true">
      <condition>
        simulation/sim-time-sec ge 185.0
        position/h-agl-ft ge 15.0
      </condition>
      <set name="ap/altitude-hold-on" value="1.0"/>
      <set name="ap/altitude-target-ft" value="2313.5"/>
    </event>

    <event name="checkpoint 30s post-handoff" persistent="false">
      <condition> simulation/sim-time-sec ge 245.0 </condition>
      <notify>
        <property> simulation/sim-time-sec </property>
        <property> position/h-agl-ft </property>
        <property> velocities/v-down-fps </property>
        <property> velocities/vt-fps </property>
        <property> attitude/pitch-rad </property>
        <property> attitude/roll-rad </property>
        <property> velocities/r-rad_sec </property>
        <property> propulsion/gearbox[0]/shaft-rpm </property>
        <property> propulsion/engine[0]/torque-lbsft </property>
        <property> propulsion/engine[2]/antitorque-ctrl-rad </property>
        <property> propulsion/engine[2]/thrust-lbs </property>
        <property> fcs/collective-cmd-norm </property>
      </notify>
    </event>

    <event name="checkpoint 60s post-handoff" persistent="false">
      <condition> simulation/sim-time-sec ge 275.0 </condition>
      <notify>
        <property> simulation/sim-time-sec </property>
        <property> position/h-agl-ft </property>
        <property> velocities/v-down-fps </property>
        <property> velocities/vt-fps </property>
        <property> attitude/pitch-rad </property>
        <property> attitude/roll-rad </property>
        <property> velocities/r-rad_sec </property>
      </notify>
    </event>

    <event name="checkpoint 120s post-handoff" persistent="false">
      <condition> simulation/sim-time-sec ge 335.0 </condition>
      <notify>
        <property> simulation/sim-time-sec </property>
        <property> position/h-agl-ft </property>
        <property> velocities/v-down-fps </property>
        <property> velocities/vt-fps </property>
        <property> attitude/pitch-rad </property>
        <property> attitude/roll-rad </property>
        <property> velocities/r-rad_sec </property>
      </notify>
    </event>

    <event name="checkpoint 300s post-handoff" persistent="false">
      <condition> simulation/sim-time-sec ge 515.0 </condition>
      <notify>
        <property> simulation/sim-time-sec </property>
        <property> position/h-agl-ft </property>
        <property> velocities/v-down-fps </property>
        <property> velocities/vt-fps </property>
        <property> attitude/pitch-rad </property>
        <property> attitude/roll-rad </property>
        <property> velocities/r-rad_sec </property>
      </notify>
    </event>

    <event name="checkpoint 450s post-handoff" persistent="false">
      <condition> simulation/sim-time-sec ge 665.0 </condition>
      <notify>
        <property> simulation/sim-time-sec </property>
        <property> position/h-agl-ft </property>
        <property> velocities/v-down-fps </property>
        <property> velocities/vt-fps </property>
        <property> attitude/pitch-rad </property>
        <property> attitude/roll-rad </property>
        <property> velocities/r-rad_sec </property>
      </notify>
    </event>

    <event name="checkpoint 600s post-handoff" persistent="false">
      <condition> simulation/sim-time-sec ge 815.0 </condition>
      <notify>
        <property> simulation/sim-time-sec </property>
        <property> position/h-agl-ft </property>
        <property> velocities/v-down-fps </property>
        <property> velocities/vt-fps </property>
        <property> attitude/pitch-rad </property>
        <property> attitude/roll-rad </property>
        <property> velocities/r-rad_sec </property>
      </notify>
    </event>

    <event name="checkpoint 750s post-handoff" persistent="false">
      <condition> simulation/sim-time-sec ge 965.0 </condition>
      <notify>
        <property> simulation/sim-time-sec </property>
        <property> position/h-agl-ft </property>
        <property> velocities/v-down-fps </property>
        <property> velocities/vt-fps </property>
        <property> attitude/pitch-rad </property>
        <property> attitude/roll-rad </property>
        <property> velocities/r-rad_sec </property>
      </notify>
    </event>

    <event name="final checkpoint 900s post-handoff" persistent="false">
      <condition> simulation/sim-time-sec ge 1114.9 </condition>
      <notify>
        <property> simulation/sim-time-sec </property>
        <property> position/h-agl-ft </property>
        <property> velocities/v-down-fps </property>
        <property> velocities/vt-fps </property>
        <property> attitude/pitch-rad </property>
        <property> attitude/roll-rad </property>
        <property> velocities/r-rad_sec </property>
        <property> propulsion/gearbox[0]/shaft-rpm </property>
        <property> propulsion/engine[0]/n1 </property>
        <property> propulsion/engine[0]/thrust-lbs </property>
      </notify>
    </event>

  </run>

</runscript>
